  "readmeFile": "NuGet.README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.1.2 (2026-10-26): patch release with no API changes - a bound text parameter is no longer re-scanned as SQL text, so a value holding an apostrophe, a doubled quote, a backslash, a comma or a parenthesis now round-trips exactly instead of landing in the neighbouring column or failing with \"Mismatched parentheses in VALUES clause\"; full detail in docs/CHANGELOG.md. Previous: v2.1.1 (2026-10-25): patch release with no API changes. A float[] parameter now reaches a VECTOR(n) column as a vector instead of the literal text \"System.Single[]\", and ORDER BY vec_distance_*() LIMIT k now reaches the vector index instead of a full scan. Previous: v2.1.0 (2026-10-10): Munarium-inspired native C# features - DiskAnn index type, content-verified artifacts (canonical manifest + SHA256 artifact_id + verification), hybrid fusion weights, C# 15 record-based BuildResult for strict error handling. All changes are pure managed .NET 11 / C# 15 on the release/v2.1.0.0 branch. See docs/Vectors/MUNARIUM_INSPIRATION_PLAN.md.",
